WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.360
What colour is the ground under

2
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:03.780
India's crops?

3
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.710
It depends on rock and rain.

4
00:00:07.281 --> 00:00:08.921
First, black soil.

5
00:00:08.921 --> 00:00:10.941
It covers most of the Deccan

6
00:00:10.941 --> 00:00:13.041
Plateau. It is clay:

7
00:00:13.041 --> 00:00:15.281
it swells when wet and cracks

8
00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.281
when dry.

9
00:00:16.281 --> 00:00:18.521
A soil that ploughs itself?

10
00:00:18.521 --> 00:00:20.561
Nearly. The cracks do the

11
00:00:20.561 --> 00:00:22.901
loosening. It holds moisture for

12
00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:25.081
a very long time, so rain fed

13
00:00:25.081 --> 00:00:27.781
crops last into the dry season.

14
00:00:27.781 --> 00:00:30.021
Its other name is black cotton

15
00:00:30.021 --> 00:00:30.911
soil.

16
00:00:31.496 --> 00:00:33.876
Red soil forms on crystalline

17
00:00:33.876 --> 00:00:35.896
rocks in the drier east and

18
00:00:35.896 --> 00:00:37.596
south of the Deccan.

19
00:00:37.596 --> 00:00:39.876
Iron gives it the colour.

20
00:00:39.876 --> 00:00:42.066
Hydrated, it looks yellow.

21
00:00:42.584 --> 00:00:44.304
Laterite comes from the Latin

22
00:00:44.304 --> 00:00:45.724
word for brick.

23
00:00:45.724 --> 00:00:48.044
Heavy tropical rain washes out

24
00:00:48.044 --> 00:00:50.604
lime and silica, and leaves iron

25
00:00:50.604 --> 00:00:51.924
and aluminium.

26
00:00:51.924 --> 00:00:54.324
It is cut into bricks, and red

27
00:00:54.324 --> 00:00:56.614
laterite suits cashew trees.

28
00:00:57.069 --> 00:00:58.229
And the biggest?

29
00:00:58.229 --> 00:01:00.936
Alluvial soil, about forty per

30
00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:03.109
cent of the country, laid down

31
00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:04.159
by rivers.

32
00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.598
What do all three lack?

33
00:01:06.598 --> 00:01:09.618
Nitrogen. Black soil also lacks

34
00:01:09.618 --> 00:01:11.798
phosphorus, and laterite,

35
00:01:11.798 --> 00:01:12.608
calcium.

36
00:01:14.089 --> 00:01:14.822
For GS1:

37
00:01:14.822 --> 00:01:17.169
black soil, the Deccan, cracks

38
00:01:17.169 --> 00:01:18.429
and moisture.

39
00:01:18.429 --> 00:01:21.649
Red, iron, east and south.

40
00:01:21.649 --> 00:01:24.129
Laterite, leaching and bricks.

41
00:01:24.129 --> 00:01:26.679
All three are poor in nitrogen.

42
00:01:27.744 --> 00:01:29.224
One country.

43
00:01:29.224 --> 00:01:31.684
Rock and rain, and a different

44
00:01:31.684 --> 00:01:33.354
ground each time.
